------------------------------------------------------------------------
SUMMARY
------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Every block vector the compositional simulator fills, at the top of the gas
-- cap (1), the two cells straddling the gas-oil contact (24 and 25), the two
-- straddling the water-oil contact (34 and 35) and the bottom of the water
-- (40), plus the field average pressure. The COMPVD table names both phases,
-- so cells 24 and 25 pin the vapour and liquid rows either side of the gas-oil
-- contact, while 34 and 35 pin the hydrocarbon-to-water transition. Nothing
-- moves over this schedule; the vectors pin the equilibrated state.

FPR

